---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import {
  captureHost,
  captureRuns,
  clientRuns,
  clientSetup,
  reproduceCapture,
} from '../../lib/benchmarks.js'

const format = (value: number) =>
  value < 10 ? value.toFixed(2) : value.toFixed(2).replace(/\.00$/u, '')
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Benchmarks · SuiteCut"
  description="Measured native CEF 156 capture throughput and native client latency, with host, workload and reproduction command."
  current="benchmarks"
>
  <article class="page prose">
    <h1>Benchmarks</h1>
    <p>
      Only the latest valid measurements on the CEF 156 engine are published. Each one names its
      commit, host and workload, and how to run it again.
    </p>

    <h2 id="recording">1080p120 recording</h2>
    <p class="muted">{captureHost}</p>
    <div class="fps">
      {
        captureRuns.map((row) => (
          <div class="fps-row">
            <span class="label">{row.run}</span>
            <span class="fps-track">
              <span class="fps-fill" style={`width:${(row.fps / 120) * 100}%`} />
            </span>
            <span class="fps-value">{row.fps.toFixed(2)}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <p class="label">Distinct frames per second, out of 120</p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Run</th>
            <th>Frames</th>
            <th>Held paints</th>
            <th>Audio</th>
            <th>Load</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            captureRuns.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{row.run}</td>
                <td>{row.frames}</td>
                <td>{row.held}</td>
                <td>{row.audio}</td>
                <td>{row.load}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Every encoded frame carried a valid paint ID with an exact timestamp. The recorder dropped and
      coalesced nothing. Held paints are frames CEF never delivered, filled by holding the previous
      image.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      The strict 120 FPS sustained gate did not pass on the 120 s and 60 s runs. The host was also
      running desktop apps beside the load workers. A run on 2026-10-20 at commit c75d579, on a
      quieter host, measured 120.00 distinct FPS over 120 s with no held paints. Whether the gap is
      contention or a regression isn't established yet.
    </p>

    <h2 id="client">Native client</h2>
    <p class="muted">{clientSetup}</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Median</th>
            <th>Native C++</th>
            <th>Node SDK</th>
            <th>Ratio</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            clientRuns.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{row.measure}</td>
                <td class="accent">
                  {format(row.native)} {row.unit}
                </td>
                <td>
                  {format(row.node)} {row.unit}
                </td>
                <td class="muted">{(row.node / row.native).toFixed(1)}×</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">
      Memory is the application client only; browser memory is excluded. These are scoped
      observations from two repetitions, not universal speedups.
    </p>

    <h2 id="reproduce">Reproduce</h2>
    <p>
      Build and relocate the macOS runtime first, then run the verifier. Add
      <code>--audio-sync-proof</code> with <code>--duration-ms 10000</code> for the A/V sync row.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock label="Terminal" code={reproduceCapture} />

    <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The recorder can't restore images CEF never delivered.</li>
      <li>
        Recording numbers are macOS ARM64 only. Intel Macs and notarized builds aren't covered.
      </li>
      <li>
        Arbitrary page workloads, popups, heavier contention and longer captures aren't qualified.
      </li>
      <li>Live streaming throughput is a separate path and isn't measured here.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      The full record is in
      <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/docs/benchmarks.md"
        >docs/benchmarks.md</a
      >
      and
      <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/native/client/VALIDATION.md"
        >native/client/VALIDATION.md</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .fps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--panel);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }

  .fps-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr 3.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .fps-track {
    position: relative;
    height: 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 99px;
    background: var(--line);
  }

  .fps-fill {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
    border-radius: 99px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .fps-value {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    font: 400 0.8125rem / 1 var(--mono);
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fps > .label {
    margin: 0;
  }

  td.accent {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
